From 280b0f472d51ff2df0230c23f187159ae57945d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 23:42:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] docs(merge): align checks_green comment with isCheckGreen
 success class

CodeRabbit #289: the doc said checks must be "SUCCESS", but the evaluator
delegates to isCheckGreen (broader green/success-class). Reworded to "green per
isCheckGreen" so operators aren't misled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/merge-rules.js | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/merge-rules.js b/lib/merge-rules.js
index 8fbdcf4c..e51c1aa1 100644
--- a/lib/merge-rules.js
+++ b/lib/merge-rules.js
@@ -124,12 +124,12 @@ function checkName(check) {
 }
 
 /**
- * `checks_green` — every CI check must be SUCCESS. Optionally scoped:
+ * `checks_green` — every CI check must be green per `isCheckGreen`. Optionally scoped:
  *   - bare string / no arg → ALL checks must be green (strict default).
  *   - { ignore: ["A","B"] } → the named checks are EXEMPT; every OTHER check
  *     must be green. `ignore: []` is identical to the bare form.
  *   - { only: ["A"] }       → ONLY the named checks must be green (present AND
- *     SUCCESS); all others are ignored.
+ *     green per `isCheckGreen`); all others are ignored.
  * `ignore` + `only` together is malformed → fail-closed. Exact name match.
  * (`required_only` — scope to the branch-protection required set — is a
  * documented follow-up, not built here.)
-- 
